000100 REM two workers wait on each other forever; main walks away
       $w1 = SPAWN hold1                       ;
       $w2 = SPAWN hold2                       ;
       PRINT "main is done. the workers are waiting on each other."
      * main stops itself. the workers keep yielding, making no progress.
      * the deadlock detector exists. it runs in a thread that is usually
      * deadlocked, so it usually misses; a watchdog cleans up after it.
       STOP
      *
hold1  YIELD
       GOTO hold1
      *
hold2  YIELD
       GOTO hold2
